meta {
  name: Leave bond
  type: http
  seq: 17
}

post {
  url: {{api}}/bonds/{{bondId}}/leave
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "withdrawEntries": false
  }
}

docs {
  Ends the bond for both of you: 204, and it is ARCHIVED from then on. Leaving twice is 409 BOND_ARCHIVED.

  The body is optional. Sent with no body at all, a leave KEEPS your entries, which is what the example here says out loud. Set "withdrawEntries" to true to take them back: your partner stops reading them at once and the rows are erased within seconds. That cannot be undone.

  The default is the opposite of Block's, which withdraws unless told not to. A misspelt key is 400 and ends nothing.
}
